  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Beejarapaga Shalemu Raju vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 3 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4873 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 & A2 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.43 of 2019 of Palamaner Urban Police Station, Chittoor District, which was registered against them for the offences under Sections 272, 273, 328 of IPC and Sec.59(1) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on credible information on 17.04.2019 at 10.30 A.M., on bypass road, at Nagamangalam, Palamaner Town, A1 and A2 were caughthold while they were illegally transporting forty gunny bags contained prohibited V-1 tobacco guthkha sachets, from Tumkur of Karnataka to Visakhapatnam for wrongful gain without any permission or any valid license for unloading on the instructions of A3 of Tumkur in the Eicher vehicle belongs to A4 and arrested the accused. Later the SI of Police registered a case against the accused in Crime No.43 of 2019 for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 & batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 & batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
